# Run Artifacts

A **run** is one bounded change from request to finished work. Artifacts live in
`doc/runs/<YYYYMMDD>-<HHMM>-<slug>-<suffix>/`. The suffix is a short random string so two
runs in the same minute cannot collide.

`doc/runs/` is never loaded wholesale. It is read only when the Coordinator hands over a
specific path.

## How many files

**`low`** — `run.md` with sections plan and report, plus three files of its own:
`request.md`, `grader.md` and `status.md`. The request is written in Step 1, before the
level is known, so its form cannot depend on the level. The gate log cannot live inside
`run.md` either: `grader.md` and `status.md` belong to the Coordinator, which writes them
from commands it ran and decisions it made itself, while `run.md` carries the work.

**`medium` and `high`** — separate files:

| File | Written by | Content |
|------|-----------|---------|
| `request.md` | Coordinator | the request in its own words |
| `change.md` | Planner | intent delta (only when the tree changed) |
| `plan.md` | Planner | goal, outputs, test spec, Definition of Done |
| `slice.md` | Coordinator | output of `intent slice` |
| `critique.md` | Critic | `ACCEPT` / `REVISE` with reasons |
| `report.md` | Coder | what was done, read, changed, decided |
| `coder-evidence.md` | Coder | raw output the Coder measured; optional, never named `grader*` |
| `grader.md` | Grader = the Coordinator itself | machine log of `VERIFY.md`, never the Coder's |
| `review.md` | Adversary | `APPROVE` / `REQUEST CHANGES` |
| `status.md` | Coordinator | final state, models, loop counts, Human gate |

## Front matter

Every artifact starts with:

```yaml
---
run_id: 20260815-1328-user-email-a7
intent_ids: ["i0042"]
role: Coder
model: <the slug actually used>
complexity: medium
status: in-progress        # in-progress | done | escalated | abandoned | awaiting-acceptance
---
```

`plan.md` (or `run.md`) additionally declares what the run is allowed to touch — the
scope guard reads exactly these two lists:

```yaml
outputs: ["src/db/models/user.py", "tests/db/test_user.py"]
incidental: ["uv.lock", "doc/intent/MAP.md"]
```

Incidental files are named **in advance**, so they cannot be added once the guard
complains. `doc/intent/_realization.yaml` is the one exception: it is always allowed,
because writing it is the recorded result of the run rather than part of its change.

## Definition of Ready — the plan is not accepted without it

- [ ] The goal is measurable, not "improve X".
- [ ] Outputs name concrete files or interfaces.
- [ ] The slice comes from `intent slice`, not from "read everything".
- [ ] Every affected contract has a named enforcer, including new ones.
- [ ] Test spec: happy path + at least one edge case + at least one error case.
      For a pure refactor: unchanged behaviour + the regression set.
- [ ] Every Definition of Done item maps to an artifact or a command.
- [ ] Incidental files are listed.
- [ ] No node in the slice has a blocking open question.
- [ ] The run is implementable and testable in isolation.

## Definition of Done — filled by the Coder, verified by the Adversary

Each item is a checkable artifact or command. Two items are mandatory:

- [ ] Failing-test evidence: the new test fails on unchanged code (`report.md`, not `grader.md`).
- [ ] `VERIFY.md` passes, including `intent validate` and `intent scope`.

Realization is not ticked by the Coder, and above `low` not by a green Grader alone either.
The **Coordinator** runs
`intent realization claim <iNNNN> --evidence doc/runs/<run> --by Coordinator` while closing
the run, once every gate the level requires has passed: at `low` the gates themselves, at
`medium` and `high` also `APPROVE` in `review.md`. A claim written by the Coder is refused
by the tool.

## Report structure

Write `report.md` prose in `<communication-language>` (see `00-communication-language.mdc`);
keep file paths, symbols and commands as they are.

| # | Section | Czech heading |
|---|---------|---------------|
| 1 | What was implemented | `## Co bylo implementováno` |
| 2 | Inputs and outputs | `## Vstupy a výstupy` |
| 3 | Methods and decisions | `## Použité metody a rozhodnutí` |
| 4 | Code references | `## Reference do kódu` |
| 5 | Evidence | `## Důkazy` |
| 6 | Definition of Done | `## Definition of Done` |

- **Inputs and outputs**: `###` subsections (Read / Created / Changed / Not touched),
  **one repo path per bullet**, always in backticks.
- **Code references**: a table `| File | Lines | Summary |`.
- **Evidence**: a table `| Command | Result | Exit code |`. Numbers written here are
  *claims*; the trustworthy record is `grader.md`.
- **Definition of Done**: a short paragraph, not a duplicated checklist.

❌ One bullet with comma-separated paths.
✅ One path per line.

## Run states

| State | Meaning | The branch |
|-------|---------|-----------|
| `in-progress` | running | kept |
| `done` | approved | ready to merge or commit |
| `escalated` | rounds exhausted or blocking finding | frozen, waiting for the Human |
| `awaiting-acceptance` | work finished, policy asks the Human to accept the node | kept until accepted |
| `abandoned` | the Human cancelled it | branch deleted, artifacts kept as audit |

## Closing a run

1. Write `status.md`: final state, models used, loop counts, Human gate decision.
2. A decision that changes boundaries or interfaces across nodes becomes an ADR in
   `doc/architecture/decisions/`, citing the short ids. It must not stay in the report.
3. Skipping the Human review is recorded, never silent:

```yaml
human_review: skipped
skipped_by: Coordinator
skip_reason: "complexity=low; grader passed; scope clean; no intent change"
```

4. Commit only when the Human asks. The message ends with `Intent: iNNNN` and
   `Run: <run_id>`.
